# SplitEase — Complete Backend Technical Specification

Scope: backend only (FastAPI core API + notification worker). Frontend excluded — build and verify entirely through Swagger UI (`/docs`) and browser  devtools against raw HTTP calls (curl/Postman/httpie also fine).

---

## 1. High-Level Architecture

```
                 ┌─────────────┐
   Client ─────▶ │  Core API   │──────▶ PostgreSQL (Cloud SQL)
 (Swagger/curl)  │  (FastAPI)  │──────▶ Redis (cache + pub/sub)
                 └─────┬───────┘
                       │ publishes events
                       ▼
                 ┌─────────────┐
                 │ Notification │
                 │   Worker     │──────▶ (logs/prints email instead
                 │ (subscriber) │         of real SMTP for v1)
                 └─────────────┘
```

Two independently deployable services sharing one Postgres instance and one Redis instance:

1. **core-api** — all synchronous REST endpoints. Owns all writes to Postgres.
2. **notification-worker** — a standalone Python process (not a web server) that subscribes to a Redis Pub/Sub channel and reacts to events (new expense, settlement made) by "sending" a notification (for v1: log it clearly, structured, as if it were an email — no real SMTP needed to prove the pattern).

They never call each other directly. All communication is core-api → Redis → worker. This is your async messaging / service-boundary story.

